/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 116 0 R
/T (Why the Mean Is Insufficient: The arithmetic mean collapses an entire distribution into a single location parameter, erasing information about variance, multimodality, and transient drops. Positive and negative deviations cancel out around 100 Mbps, allowing an unstable access point swinging between 70 Mbps and 130 Mbps to report the exact same 100 Mbps average as a rock-steady link. )
/E (Why the Mean Is Insufficient: The arithmetic mean collapses an entire distribution into a single location parameter, erasing information about variance, multimodality, and transient drops. Positive and negative deviations cancel out around 100 Mbps, allowing an unstable access point swinging between 70 Mbps and 130 Mbps to report the exact same 100 Mbps average as a rock-steady link. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
