/T (What Decision-Makers Can and Cannot Conclude: Security leadership CAN conclude that anomalous outbound byte spikes and ICMP traffic concentration are high-precision indicators of malicious activity requiring immediate rate-limiting and deep packet inspection. Leadership CANNOT conclude that low-byte UDP flows are inherently benign \(as DNS amplification or C2 beacons may use small payloads\) or that protocol choice alone causes attacks. )
/E (What Decision-Makers Can and Cannot Conclude: Security leadership CAN conclude that anomalous outbound byte spikes and ICMP traffic concentration are high-precision indicators of malicious activity requiring immediate rate-limiting and deep packet inspection. Leadership CANNOT conclude that low-byte UDP flows are inherently benign \(as DNS amplification or C2 beacons may use small payloads\) or that protocol choice alone causes attacks. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [41]
>>
