1018 0 obj
<<
/Title (Three Non-Obvious EDA Observations: \(1\) Src_Bytes is heavily right-skewed \(overall mean = 1,431 bytes vs. median = 885 bytes, skewness = 2.71\), driven by heavy-tailed attack payloads. \(2\) While TCP accounts for the largest volume of total traffic \(55%\), ICMP exhibitsthehighest conditional attack rate \(72.1% Attack vs. 44.3% TCP and 15.2% UDP\). \(3\) Flow duration separatessharply by transport state: TCP handshakes/streams average 419.6 ms compared to 187.4 ms for UDP and 68.2msfor ICMP.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 876 0 R
/Next 1019 0 R
>>
endobj
1019 0 obj
<<
/Title (Stage 4 Pre-Test Predictions \(Recorded Prior toFormalTesting\): \(P1\) Q1 will be statistically significant because Figure 6 \(top-right\) shows the Attack median andIQRsitting well above Normal traffic. \(P2\) Q2 will be statistically significant because protocol boxplots\(bottom-left\) display clear vertical separation in median duration. \(P3\) Q3 will show a significant associationbecause stacked bar proportions \(bottom-right\) vary sharply from 72.1% Attack in ICMP down to 15.2%inUDP.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 876 0 R
/Prev 1018 0 R
>>
endobj
