/Title (When SD and IQR Disagree: Config C illustrates this exact divergence: its IQR is small \(4.30 Mbps\) because the middle 50% of traffic is stable, whereas its SD is huge \(11.63 Mbps\) because squared deviations heavily penalize the 60 Mbps dropout outliers. Relying on IQR alone would hide the dropout attacks.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1258 0 R
/Prev 1307 0 R
/First 1338 0 R
