1309 0 obj
<<
/Title (When Config C is reassigned to low-power IoT sensors operating at a 20 Mbpstarget \(simulated via set.seed\(25\) with baseline 20 Mbps, SD = 0.8 Mbps, and 8.3% dropouts around 12 Mbps\),comparing raw standard deviations becomes invalid because a 2.5 Mbps spread around 20 Mbps represents a massive 12.5% fluctuation, whereas 2.05 Mbps around 100 Mbps is only 2.04%.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1282 0 R
/Next 1310 0 R
>>
endobj
1310 0 obj
<<
/Title (Relative Comparison via CV: Config A achieves CV = 2.04%, Config B achieves CV = 9.26%, and Config C \(IoT\) yields SD = 2.45 Mbps around Mean = 19.36 Mbps, giving CV = 12.64%. Even after normalizing for the lower IoT target, Config C exhibits the worst relative instability \(12.64% vs. 2.04%\), proving that relative consistency and policy adherence govern wireless reliability far more than raw mean throughput.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1282 0 R
/Prev 1309 0 R
>>
